# Line endings, for a repository developed on Windows and deployed on Linux.
#
# Two things were true before this file existed, and both cost real time.
#
# The working tree is CRLF and the committed blobs are LF, so the Windows git
# and the WSL git in the same working copy disagreed about whether anything had
# changed: WSL's reported 289 files modified on a clean tree, measured
# 2026-09-27. `text=auto` normalises the index to LF and normalises the working
# tree before comparing it, so both gits see the same tree. It rewrites nothing
# that is already committed.
* text=auto

# A shell script is read by bash, where a trailing CR is not whitespace but part
# of the command name: `set -euo pipefail` with a trailing CR parses as an
# unknown command. deploy/cloud/certs.sh failed exactly this way during the
# Phase 7 walk (this repository's PR #3), and deploy/build-images.sh needs its
# CRs stripped before it will run on a fresh checkout. Forcing LF in the working
# tree stops that depending on the setting of whichever git checked the file
# out. deploy/cloud/.gitattributes already forces LF for that whole subtree,
# because it is read inside Linux containers; this rule is the general case.
*.sh text eol=lf
